          "summary": "Customer owns Developed Software it pays for; M&I retains and licenses back its pre-existing/generic IP",
          "comment": "[Playbook] We cannot accept that work of authorship we pay for becomes M&I's property with only a Term-limited right of use under 17.2, so we have flipped ownership of Customer-funded Developed Software to us while confirming M&I keeps its pre-existing and generic tools, know-how and platform. If M&I prefers to retain title, we can instead take a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free licence to use, modify and sublicense the Developed Software we funded.",
